WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.513
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:15.948
Unit seven: Past Perfect Continuous. Today you will explain the cause of a past situation.

4
00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:18.773
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:23.071
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:24.744
Had been.

7
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.876
Had been means the helper of the past perfect continuous.

8
00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:30.786
I had been working.

9
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:33.838
Your turn. Say: Had been.

10
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.562
Had been.

11
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:38.958
-ing.

12
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.867
-ing means the verb ending for continuous forms.

13
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:44.647
Studying, working.

14
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.403
Your turn. Say: -ing.

15
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:50.943
-ing.

16
00:00:51.683 --> 00:00:53.311
Duration before past.

17
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:57.617
Duration before past means how long before a past moment.

18
00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:59.682
The duration was long.

19
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:03.632
Your turn. Say: Duration before past.

20
00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:08.292
Duration before past.

21
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.469
Continuous action.

22
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:14.563
Continuous action means an action with no clear end.

23
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.859
A continuous action.

24
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.311
Your turn. Say: Continuous action.

25
00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.621
Continuous action.

26
00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:26.791
Ongoing past.

27
00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:31.339
Ongoing past means continuing before another past event.

28
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.880
An ongoing past activity.

29
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:37.426
Your turn. Say: Ongoing past.

30
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.581
Ongoing past.

31
00:01:42.317 --> 00:01:44.049
Before another past event.

32
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:48.396
Before another past event means earlier than a past moment.

33
00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:50.368
Before the call came.

34
00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:54.379
Your turn. Say: Before another past event.

35
00:01:57.233 --> 00:01:59.244
Before another past event.

36
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:01.159
Long action.

37
00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:05.055
Long action means an activity lasting some time.

38
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.965
A long action.

39
00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:10.353
Your turn. Say: Long action.

40
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.410
Long action.

41
00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:15.965
Cause.

42
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.973
Cause means the reason for a result.

43
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.060
The cause was clear.

44
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.151
Your turn. Say: Cause.

45
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.885
Cause.

46
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:32.629
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:33.483 --> 00:02:36.075
Visal, why were you tired yesterday evening?

48
00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:47.571
I was tired because I had been studying since morning. The past perfect continuous explains the cause of a past situation. It is had been plus the -ing form.

49
00:02:48.683 --> 00:02:50.950
How is it different from the past perfect?

50
00:02:52.050 --> 00:03:07.964
The continuous focuses on duration or the process: I had been waiting for an hour. The simple form focuses on completion: I had waited and then I left. State verbs prefer the simple form.

51
00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:11.247
What time expressions do we use?

52
00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:26.194
For and since show the duration before the past moment: They had been living there since 2010 when the flood happened. The result is often something we can see, such as tiredness or wet clothes.

53
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:29.031
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:29.883 --> 00:03:35.285
Grammar focus: Past perfect continuous: had been plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:35.585 --> 00:03:36.760
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.204
I was tired because I had been studying since morning.

57
00:03:41.117 --> 00:03:43.081
She had been waiting for an hour.

58
00:03:43.983 --> 00:03:46.517
They had been living there since 2010.

59
00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:55.178
Use had been + verb-ing to show an action in progress for some time before a past moment, often explaining the cause of a past situation.

60
00:03:55.917 --> 00:04:00.264
Be careful! Don't say: I was tired; I studied all day.

61
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.105
Say: I was tired; I had been studying all day.

62
00:04:05.405 --> 00:04:06.940
Use had been + -ing.

63
00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:10.885
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.131
The Cause Behind It.

65
00:04:13.431 --> 00:04:16.591
I was exhausted because I had been studying since morning.

66
00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.470
She had been waiting for an hour when the bus finally arrived.

67
00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:24.302
The ground was wet because it had been raining all night.

68
00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.217
They had been living in that house for years before the storm.

69
00:04:29.233 --> 00:04:31.244
The long action explained the result.

70
00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:36.440
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:37.283 --> 00:04:39.538
She was tired because she blank all day.

72
00:04:39.838 --> 00:04:43.573
A, had been working. B, has been working. C, was worked.

73
00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:49.435
The answer is A: had been working.

74
00:04:50.583 --> 00:04:53.187
The ground was wet; it blank all night.

75
00:04:53.487 --> 00:04:57.175
A, had been raining. B, was rained. C, has rained.

76
00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:03.000
The answer is A: had been raining.

77
00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.033
Which focuses on duration?

78
00:05:06.333 --> 00:05:10.184
A, had been waiting. B, had waited. C, waited.

79
00:05:13.733 --> 00:05:15.861
The answer is A: had been waiting.

80
00:05:17.017 --> 00:05:18.134
Which is correct?

81
00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:24.270
A, I had been knowing him for years.. B, I had known him for years.. C, I had been know him..

82
00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:30.692
The answer is B: I had known him for years..

83
00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.372
According to the reading, why was the ground wet?

84
00:05:34.672 --> 00:05:39.335
A, it rained all night. B, a pipe broke. C, someone washed it.

85
00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.109
The answer is A: it rained all night.

86
00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.544
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:53.405
Write a sentence using the past perfect continuous.

88
00:06:02.217 --> 00:06:03.705
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:04.005 --> 00:06:17.992
When I arrived at the airport, my friends were exhausted because they had been travelling for fourteen hours. They had been waiting for me since morning. I use the past perfect continuous to show the duration and cause.

90
00:06:18.292 --> 00:06:19.966
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:26.695
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past perfect continuous: had been plus verb-ing.

92
00:06:26.995 --> 00:06:30.518
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

93
00:06:30.818 --> 00:06:33.505
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:33.805 --> 00:06:37.456
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

